-- title:
--   The pipeline with three separate computed values (round six, `pipeline_err3`)
-- statement:
--   **The pipeline with three separate computed values** (per-call procedures): `U ≈ F u`,
--   `V ≈ F v`, and `Z ≈ F(conj z)` for `z = Q_p(U V)`.
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.KFZChirpR`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem NLogN.KFZ.pipeline_err3 {κ : Type*} [Fintype κ] (p : ℕ) {F : (κ → ℂ) → (κ → ℂ)} (hF : LinC F)
--       (Es : ℝ) (hEs : Es * hp p ≤ 1 / 100) {u v : κ → ℂ} (hu1 : ‖u‖ ≤ 1 / 4) (hv1 : ‖v‖ ≤ 1 / 4)
--       {U V Z : κ → ℂ} (hU : ‖U - F u‖ ≤ Es * hp p) (hV : ‖V - F v‖ ≤ Es * hp p)
--       (hZ : ‖Z - F (cnj (QA p (U * V)))‖ ≤ Es * hp p) :
--       Grid p (QA p (U * V)) ∧ ‖QA p (U * V)‖ ≤ 1 / 2 ∧
--       ‖cnj Z - cnj (F (cnj (F u * F v)))‖ ≤ (3 * Es + 2) * hp p
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** KFZ: the per-call form of the chirp interface
--
--   `ChirpNeed` fixes `M̃r` per `n` before the input and the machine state, and asks the procedure to
--   output exactly `C̃(x) = chirpT p (mcT p M̃r θ̃ θ̃⁻) b̃ ã x`. With `P18IL` as the only source of
--   `M̃r`, this cannot be met. `P18IL` gives, for each initial state `encK s f` (unmanaged part `s`,
--   tail `l` on stack `0`), *some* run with *some* result `zh` within the Prop 18 bound. Nothing ties
--   the results of two different states together, and a `P18IL` procedure may legally read `s` or `l`
--   and restore it. The dependence on the input tape `Isym` can be removed (`KFZIsym`); the dependence
--   on `s` and `l` cannot. The obvious workaround, computing `mrX` exactly, is an integer product of
--   size `Θ(V)` and does not fit the `V · Ncost · polylog` budget.
--
--   This file gives the per-call statement and shows that it gives the chain everything it uses:
--
--   * **`ChirpNeedR`**: `ChirpNeed` with `∃ Mrt` (and its `ErC · hp` bound) moved after the input. The
--     tables `θ̃, θ̃⁻, ã, b̃` and `ζ` stay fixed per `n` (they are explicit FM table outputs).
--   * **`ChirpNeed.toR`**: `ChirpNeed → ChirpNeedR`.
--   * **`chirp_call_err`**: for any `M̃r` with the Prop 18 bound and the fixed tables, one call
--     satisfies `‖C̃ x − Q F_t x‖ ≤ (Er + 22) hp`, `‖C̃ x‖ ≤ 1`, `Grid p (C̃ x)`. These are exactly the
--     conclusions `chain_close` uses about the chirp step (its `hCt`).
--   * **`pipeline_err3`**: `pipeline_err` with three separate computed values `F̃u`, `F̃v`, `F̃(z̄)`
--     instead of one
--
